---
/*
  About us page (The Program): Erin's story, from her draft wording
  (DRAFT WORDING, "About us"). Spelling fixed and hyphens turned into dashes;
  otherwise her words as written.
*/
import SectionLayout from '../layouts/SectionLayout.astro';
---

<SectionLayout href="/about/">
  <p>
    Hello, my name is Erin and I am living with brain cancer. I was diagnosed after suffering out of
    the blue seizures in late 2022. Only 3 months after giving birth to my daughter and days after
    celebrating my son’s 2nd birthday, my whole life changed forever.
  </p>
  <p>
    I received brain surgery just before Christmas followed by radiation and chemotherapy. As these
    treatments tend to do, I was left with a score book of mental and physical side effects, impacting
    my life short term as well as long term.
  </p>
  <p>
    Finding myself trying to lighten the load for those around me, I desperately sought connection
    with someone who understood what I was living. This propelled me to make a Facebook page local to
    my home so I could meet others in person for a coffee or walk to help. Soon the group had over 100
    members with different cancer types, ages, genders and situations. We shared anything and
    everything we wanted in a safe space and were regularly meeting up, opening up and sharing our
    loads.
  </p>
  <p>
    Along the way I realised the knowledge that was being passed around was extremely useful,
    important and comforting and I started piecing it all together for others that needed it.
  </p>
  <p>
    Now here we are! Sharing our collective information far and wide with understanding, empathy and
    most importantly, humour!
  </p>
</SectionLayout>
